name: NordVPN (WireGuard)
group: extras
what: NordVPN servers in several countries as built-in network connections, with a tray icon. Survives SteamOS updates.
why: The usual NordVPN install goes into `/usr`, which every SteamOS update wipes, and the Frame's desktop has no network applet to switch VPNs.
changes: `nordvpn-wg`, tray app, KDE autostart entry
access: **Outside your home folder:** NetworkManager WireGuard connections (via `nmcli`)
survives-updates: Yes (its connections live in NetworkManager's settings, which updates keep)
undo: `./install.sh uninstall nordvpn`
